---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TimelineItem from '../../components/ui/TimelineItem.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Gatherings & Workshops — ${SITE.name}`}
  description="Guided workshops for grief and healing, led by Ajai Blue-Saunders."
>
  <section class="section stack stack-loose">
    <div class="section-heading-row">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Gatherings</p>
        <h1>Guided sessions for grief and healing.</h1>
        <p>
          Led by Ajai Blue-Saunders, these workshops blend faith, herbal wisdom, and grief
          education to help widows heal in body, mind, and spirit.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img src="/images/dove-hands.png" alt="" class="section-motif" width="289" height="342" />
    </div>
    <ol class="timeline">
      <TimelineItem title="Common Remedies to Stay Strong in the Midst of Your Grief Journey">
        <p class="timeline-scripture">
          "He heals the brokenhearted and binds up their wounds." — Psalm 147:3
        </p>
        <p>
          Grief is not just emotional — it impacts your sleep, immune system, digestion, memory,
          mood, and even your ability to make simple decisions. In this restorative and
          faith-centered workshop, we uncover how grief affects the whole body and explore
          practical, holistic remedies that support healing from the inside out. This workshop
          offers encouragement and tools to help you remain strong — spiritually, emotionally, and
          physically — while allowing God's healing balm to minister to every wounded place.
        </p>
      </TimelineItem>
      <TimelineItem title="What's the Real Tea?">
        <p class="timeline-scripture">
          "The leaves of the tree are for the healing of the nations." — Revelation 22:2
        </p>
        <p>
          There's wisdom steeped in every cup. "What's the Real Tea?" invites you to discover the
          power of natural herbal teas for every season of life — grief, stress, immunity, rest,
          and renewal. Whether you're seeking comfort, clarity, or immune support, this workshop
          equips you with simple, effective, God-created remedies to nourish body and spirit — one
          cup at a time.
        </p>
      </TimelineItem>
      <TimelineItem title="Natural Cures for Jangled Nerves">
        <p class="timeline-scripture">
          "You will keep in perfect peace those whose minds are steadfast, because they trust in
          You." — Isaiah 26:3
        </p>
        <p>
          Anxiety, racing thoughts, tension, and overwhelm can feel relentless — especially after
          loss. This empowering workshop focuses on proven, natural ways to calm your nervous
          system, sharpen your focus, and reclaim your peace. You'll leave with actionable
          strategies to soothe "jangled nerves," quiet mental chatter, and cultivate a steady,
          anchored mind rooted in God's peace.
        </p>
      </TimelineItem>
      <TimelineItem title="The Widow's Bill of Rights">
        <p class="timeline-scripture">
          "Above all else, guard your heart, for everything you do flows from it." — Proverbs 4:23
        </p>
        <p>
          "You're still grieving?" "At least he's in a better place." "God must have needed
          another angel." Widows often face a second battle — navigating unhelpful comments,
          unsolicited advice, and unrealistic expectations. This engaging and interactive workshop
          equips you with emotional tools and spiritual armor to distinguish supportive help from
          harmful words. You'll leave fortified, confident, and empowered — with clarity about your
          rights, your voice, and your healing timeline.
        </p>
      </TimelineItem>
      <TimelineItem title="Jeremiah 29:11 — Using Scripture to Heal">
        <p class="timeline-scripture">
          "For I know the plans I have for you… plans to prosper you and not to harm you, plans to
          give you hope and a future." — Jeremiah 29:11
        </p>
        <p>
          This beloved and often-quoted scripture is frequently shared during times of grief — but
          what did it truly mean in its original context? And how does it genuinely apply to loss,
          suffering, and restoration? Rather than using scripture as a quick bandage, this session
          invites deeper understanding — revealing how God's plans include hope even in seasons we
          never would have chosen.
        </p>
      </TimelineItem>
    </ol>
    <img
      src="/images/woman-tea-cup.jpg"
      alt="A woman holding a warm cup of tea in quiet reflection"
      class="photo-frame photo-frame--compact photo-frame--even-gap-loose"
      width="1280"
      height="857"
    />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
